# This file exists to be present, not to exclude much.
#
# With no .npmignore, npm falls back to .gitignore when packing. .gitignore
# deliberately excludes build output that is not source but IS part of the
# published package:
#
#   stories/assets/scss/generated/_tokens-*.scss
#       generated by `yarn build:tokens` and @imported by
#       stories/assets/scss/_variables.scss -- without them not one of the
#       packaged SCSS entry points compiles
#   stories/assets/css/style*.css
#       the compiled stylesheets a CSS-only consumer takes
#
# That fallback applies even to paths listed in package.json "files": a
# directory entry there is still filtered by the ignore rules. Having this
# file at all stops npm reading .gitignore, so the built artifacts ship.
#
# Positive selection (and the __tests__ exclusion) lives in package.json
# "files". Add exclusions there, not here -- "files" wins over this file.
